Notebook[{Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Evolution on OEIS sequences", "Title"], 
     Cell["A working notebook for the evolutionary searches. Every search \
sees the first eight terms of a sequence and is judged on the terms after \
them. Evaluate the Setup section first; every other section can then be run \
and changed on its own.", "Text"]}, Open]], 
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Setup", "Section"], 
     Cell["Load the paclet from this checkout, and the measurements.", 
      "Text"], Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[Notebo\
okDirectory[]], \
\"Recursor\"}]];\n\nNeeds[\"WolframInstitute`Recursor`\"]\n\ndata = \
Import[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"docs\", \
\"notes\", \"data\", \"OEISSynthesisAndEvolution.json.gz\"}], {\"GZIP\", \
\"RawJSON\"}];\n\narms = Association[#Name -> # & /@ \
data[\"Arms\"]];\n\noptions = data[\"Protocol\"][\"SearchOptions\"];", 
      "Code"], Cell["The improved search: every term is a test, parents are \
chosen by lexicase selection, and no two individuals behave alike. Change it \
and run it below.", "Text"], Cell["(* An evolutionary search with the \
proposal budget of EvolveRecursor in corpus v1 (24 initial\n   programs, then \
generations of 22 children) and these changes, following the program \
synthesis\n   literature:\n   1. Every training term is a test that a program \
passes or fails. Fitness is the number passed.\n   2. Lexicase selection: a \
parent is drawn from the programs that pass the tests taken in a random\n     \
 order, so a program that alone gets some term right is kept even when its \
count is low.\n   3. One individual per distinct list of values: the \
population holds no duplicate behaviour.\n   4. Variation by small additions \
and deletions (wrap a subtree in an operation, replace a subtree\n      by a \
small one, or by one of its own parts), with crossover only now and then.\n   \
5. Half of the first population are simple fixed programs; half are random.\n \
  6. A program whose values match after scaling and shifting is completed \
with that scale and shift.\n   Programs are made with the paclet's \
RandomRecursor, MutateRecursor, CrossoverRecursor,\n   RecursorSites and \
ReplaceRecursorPart. *)\n\nsimplePrograms = {Var, Succ[Var], Pred[Var], \
Half[Var], Add[Var, Var], Mul[Var, Var], Succ[Succ[Var]], Mul[Var, \
Succ[Var]],\n\tMul[Const[3], Var], Half[Mul[Var, Var]], Mul[Var, Mul[Var, \
Var]], Rem[Var, Const[2]]};\n\naffineProgram[program_, scale_, shift_] := \
With[{scaled = If[scale === 1, program, Mul[Const[scale], \
program]]},\n\tWhich[shift > 0, Add[scaled, Const[shift]], shift < 0, \
Monus[scaled, Const[-shift]], True, scaled]\n]\n\n(* scale and shift taking \
the values to the targets, or None *)\naffineFit[values_, targets_] := \
Module[{at, scale, shift},\n\tIf[! FreeQ[values, Except[_Integer], {1}], \
Return[None]];\n\tat = FirstPosition[Differences[values], _?(# =!= 0 &), \
None, {1}, Heads -> False];\n\tIf[at === None, Return[None]];\n\tat = \
First[at];\n\tIf[! Divisible[targets[[at + 1]] - targets[[at]], values[[at + \
1]] - values[[at]]], Return[None]];\n\tscale = Quotient[targets[[at + 1]] - \
targets[[at]], values[[at + 1]] - values[[at]]];\n\tshift = First[targets] - \
scale First[values];\n\tIf[scale >= 1 && scale values + shift === targets && \
! (scale === 1 && shift === 0), {scale, shift}, None]\n]\n\n(* one small \
change: wrap a subtree, replace it by a small random program, or by one of \
its parts *)\nwraps = {Succ[#1] &, Pred[#1] &, Half[#1] &, Add[#1, #2] &, \
Mul[#1, #2] &, Monus[#1, #2] &, Monus[#2, #1] &, Quot[#1, #2] &, Rem[#1, #2] \
&};\nvary[program_, maximumNodes_, randomOptions_] := Module[{sites = \
RecursorSites[program], site, small, changed},\n\tsite = \
RandomChoice[sites];\n\tsmall = RandomRecursor[RandomInteger[1], Sequence @@ \
randomOptions];\n\tchanged = Switch[RandomInteger[{1, 3}],\n\t\t1, \
ReplaceRecursorPart[program, site[\"Path\"], \
RandomChoice[wraps][site[\"Expression\"], small]],\n\t\t2, \
ReplaceRecursorPart[program, site[\"Path\"], small],\n\t\t3, With[{parts = \
Cases[site[\"Expression\"], _Symbol | _Const | _[__], {1}]},\n\t\t\tIf[parts \
=== {}, program, ReplaceRecursorPart[program, site[\"Path\"], \
RandomChoice[parts]]]]\n\t];\n\tIf[RecursorProgramQ[changed] && \
RecursorNodeCount[changed] <= maximumNodes, changed, \
program]\n]\n\nimprovedEvolve[examples_, options_, seed_] := \
BlockRandom[SeedRandom[seed]; Module[{\n\tinputs = examples[[All, 1]], \
targets = examples[[All, 2]], populationSize, generations, elites, \
maximumNodes, mutationDepth,\n\trandomOptions, evaluationOptions, values, \
individual, complete, rank, select, breed, distinct, population, best, \
history, proposals = 0\n},\n\t{populationSize, generations, elites, \
maximumNodes, mutationDepth} =\n\t\tLookup[options, {\"PopulationSize\", \
\"MaxGenerations\", \"EliteCount\", \"MaxNodes\", \
\"MutationDepth\"}];\n\trandomOptions = FilterRules[Normal[options], \
Options[RandomRecursor]];\n\tevaluationOptions = FilterRules[Normal[options], \
Options[EvaluateRecursor]];\n\tvalues[program_] := values[program] = \
Quiet[EvaluateRecursor[program, #, Sequence @@ evaluationOptions] & /@ \
inputs];\n\tcomplete[program_] := With[{fit = affineFit[values[program], \
targets]},\n\t\tIf[fit === None || RecursorNodeCount[program] + 4 > \
maximumNodes, program, affineProgram[program, First[fit], \
Last[fit]]]\n\t];\n\tindividual[candidate_] := With[{program = \
complete[candidate]},\n\t\tproposals++;\n\t\tWith[{passed = \
Boole[MapThread[SameQ, {values[program], targets}]]},\n\t\t\t<|\"Program\" -> \
program, \"Values\" -> values[program], \"Size\" -> \
RecursorNodeCount[program], \"Passed\" -> passed, \"Matches\" -> \
Total[passed]|>\n\t\t]\n\t];\n\trank[one_] := {one[\"Matches\"], \
-one[\"Size\"]};\n\tselect[pool_] := Module[{rest = \
pool},\n\t\tDo[\n\t\t\tWith[{passing = Select[rest, #[\"Passed\"][[case]] === \
1 &]}, If[passing =!= {}, rest = passing]];\n\t\t\tIf[Length[rest] === 1, \
Break[]],\n\t\t\t{case, \
RandomSample[Range[Length[inputs]]]}\n\t\t];\n\t\tRandomChoice[rest]\n\t];\n\
\tbreed[pool_] := Module[{child = \
select[pool][\"Program\"]},\n\t\tIf[RandomReal[] < 0.2, child = \
CrossoverRecursor[child, select[pool][\"Program\"], \"MaxNodes\" -> \
maximumNodes]];\n\t\tDo[child = vary[child, maximumNodes, randomOptions], \
{RandomInteger[{1, 2}]}];\n\t\tIf[RandomReal[] < 0.2, child = \
MutateRecursor[child, mutationDepth, Sequence @@ \
randomOptions]];\n\t\tindividual[child]\n\t];\n\tdistinct[pool_] := \
Values[GroupBy[ReverseSortBy[pool, rank], #[\"Values\"] &, \
First]];\n\tpopulation = distinct[individual /@ \
Join[\n\t\tTake[simplePrograms, UpTo[Quotient[populationSize, \
2]]],\n\t\tTable[RandomRecursor[Lookup[options, \"InitialDepth\"], Sequence \
@@ randomOptions], {populationSize - Min[Length[simplePrograms], \
Quotient[populationSize, 2]]}]\n\t]];\n\tbest = First[MaximalBy[population, \
rank]];\n\thistory = {best[\"Matches\"]};\n\tDo[\n\t\tpopulation = \
distinct[Join[Take[ReverseSortBy[population, rank], UpTo[elites]], \
Table[breed[population], {populationSize - elites}]]];\n\t\tbest = \
First[MaximalBy[Append[population, best], rank]];\n\t\tAppendTo[history, \
best[\"Matches\"]],\n\t\t{generations}\n\t];\n\t<|\"Program\" -> \
best[\"Program\"], \"Fitness\" -> best[\"Matches\"], \"FitnessHistory\" -> \
history, \"Proposals\" -> proposals|>\n]]", "Code"], 
     Cell["The guided search is in the paclet: EvolveRecursor with Method -> \
\"Guided\". Each variation runs a program backwards from the terms and asks a \
library of small programs for the part that is missing.", "Text"], 
     Cell["guidedSearch[examples_, seed_ : 9101] := EvolveRecursor[examples, \
Method -> \"Guided\", Sequence @@ Normal[options], \"StopOnSolve\" -> False, \
\"RandomSeed\" -> seed]", "Code"]}, Closed]], 
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["The arms", "Section"], Cell["Sequences fitted \
(the eight terms reproduced), predicted (the terms up to the twentieth too) \
and complete (every recorded term). An arm with twenty training terms has \
nothing between fitted and complete.", "Text"], Cell["counts[arm_Association] \
:= <|\"Sequences\" -> arm[\"Sequences\"], \"Fitted\" -> \
Total[arm[\"Fitted\"]],\n\t\"Predicted\" -> If[arm[\"TrainingTerms\"] === 8, \
Total[arm[\"Predicted\"]], Missing[\"NotApplicable\"]], \"Complete\" -> \
Total[arm[\"Complete\"]],\n\t\"Seconds per sequence\" -> \
Round[Mean[arm[\"Seconds\"]], 0.1]|>", "Code"], 
